<BaseLayout title="Seats and controls">
  <h1>Seats and controls</h1>
  <p>This page is an index to the driver's seating position, seat adjustment, steering-wheel controls, mirrors, windows, and common cabin switches. Exact equipment can vary with the car's option packages.</p>

  <h2>Driver position</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Adjust the seat so the pedals can be operated fully without stretching and the driver's back remains supported.</li>
    <li>Set the steering wheel so the instrument display remains visible and the wheel can be held comfortably with slightly bent arms.</li>
    <li>Adjust mirrors after the seat and steering wheel are set.</li>
    <li>Confirm that the seat and steering wheel are locked before driving.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Power seat and memory</h2>
  <p>If the vehicle is equipped with power-seat memory, use the seat controls and memory buttons as described in the owner's manual for the exact seat version. Keep hands and objects clear of moving seat mechanisms. Do not assume that every market or trim has identical memory functions.</p>

  <h2>Steering wheel and driver controls</h2>
  <p>The steering wheel provides access to driving-related and infotainment controls. Become familiar with the button layout while parked; control assignments can depend on the display and software configuration.</p>

  <h2>Restraints and airbags</h2>
  <p>Never place accessories, covers, or objects where they could interfere with seat-mounted side airbags, curtain airbags, belt operation, or the driver's ability to control the vehicle. Follow Volvo's instructions for child restraints and occupant seating positions.</p>

  <h2>Reference source</h2>
  <p>See the <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/18w46">Volvo S60 owner's information</a> for the official control descriptions and safety instructions.</p>
</BaseLayout>
